 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "A grep for `opens|starConvex` under `Geodesic/Normal/` finds `opens` only in `Basic.lean`, `Metric.lean` (as a type of points) and `BlowUp.lean` (`hU.starConvex_opens` and `v : hU.opens`). None of these unfold the body. `zero_mem_opens` (Basic.lean:172-174) converts membership by hand with `rw [\u2190 SetLike.mem_coe, coe_opens]`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Geometry/Manifold/Riemannian/Geodesic/Normal/Basic.lean",
   "fix": "Remove `@[expose]` and prove `coe_opens` with `:= (rfl)`. Add `@[simp] theorem mem_opens : x \u2208 h.opens \u2194 x \u2208 U := Iff.rfl` and use it in `zero_mem_opens` and wherever `v.2` is turned into membership in `U`.",
   "issue": "`IsNormalDomain.opens` is still `@[expose]`. The reasons given in the thread no longer apply: `Normal/BlowUp.lean` states its results with `hU.starConvex_opens` (lines 69, 80), and the origin point is built from `zero_mem_opens`. The only code that unfolds `opens` (for example `\u27e8v, v.2\u27e9` in `contMDiff_riemannianExp_comp_val`) is in this same module. There is also no `mem_opens` lemma, which is what consumers need instead of unfolding.",
   "line": 163
  }
